    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1029">

                <pb facs="1136" n="1040" xml:id="pg1040"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. Woodford.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>With reference to the first part of the Saturday memorandum, you may explain that
                    the captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> merely sought permission
                    to employ small explosive charges on upper works, to clear away wreckage and get
                    at bodies and guns, but finding his request misunderstood and opposed, he
                    withdrew it, under instructions from the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
